(also  known as on some systems) is a daemon invoked at boot time
to implement Multicast DNS and DNS Service Discovery.  On Mac  OS
X  10.6  (Snow  Leopard), is also the system‐wide Unicast DNS Re‐
solver.  listens on UDP port 5353 for Multicast DNS  Query  pack‐
ets.   When it receives a query for which it knows an answer, is‐
sues the appropriate Multicast DNS Reply packet.   also  performs
Unicast  and Multicast DNS Queries on behalf of client processes,
and maintains a cache of the replies.   has  no  user‐specifiable
command‐line  argument, and users should not run manually.  There
are several methods with which to examine internal state for  de‐
bugging  and diagnostic purposes.  The logging levels map as fol‐
lows: By default, only log level Error is logged.  A SIGUSR1 sig‐
nal toggles additional logging, with Warning and  Notice  enabled
by  default:  A  SIGUSR2 signal toggles packet logging: A SIGINFO
signal will dump a snapshot summary of the internal state to  For
